        "sourceId": 831,
        "text": "\"We must make sure that the war against extremism is overcome. We are here to win that battle.\" Mr Hidges will not be given the task of signing legislation to officially end the war against extremism but the Prime Minister is already taking the first step. Mr Hidges also acknowledged the need for a fight over the stay of South Africa's human rights law. \"The law is a question of politics,\" Mr Hidges said. \"We need politicians to do it. But it is impossible. We are in some extremely difficult situation. \"We have to come back together to fight for all human rights. \"You know, there are people who can stand up and fight. They need help. \"And if they do, this will not happen.\" Topic: defence-and-safety, australia First posted Will the Cleveland Cavaliers make a push around the free market with the announcement they are signing NBA All-Star Forward Brandon Westrow? It's good to see Westrow return to the free, but it's hard to see how he will have the tools to replace the foundation he was given by the Cavaliers over the past few seasons. Aaron Pentry, Brandon Green, Omar Allen and others will be on this list, as Westrow continues to be a big, talented forward who will use those abilities to win the ball around him. He also will have a very good shot with all of his skills aside from throwing him in the air. Going forward, Westrow will get better at playing around the court and on the bench simply because of the amount of potential he will likely bring to the table at the free market. Westrow is still just 6-years old and could be viewed as some kind of forward who can unlock his chances early in the short term and hold his edge for the long term. Here are the key free agent spots for Westrow in the 2017 Western Conference Draft: Center: DeManael Edward is a fourth-round 1st pick out of Toronto Raptors. Edward has the offensive vision and on-court skills to contribute to Cleveland's championship team, but he showed a particularly poor performance for the team thus far this season. He has a good passing game, and a great ability to move right down the court as an offensive player. Edward has given the Cavaliers much athletic talent to play throughout his career. He has an honest player vision and an athletic personality that can go head-to-header for the team and help them win games. It's often hard to see how the Cavaliers would pick a highly talented forward, like a gold medalist, or just the type of forward who likes throwing men in the air. Let's look at a forward with a well-adsured defensive game that will fit the Cavaliers' needs heading into the 2017 Western Conference Draft. Center: Michael Jones is a fifth-round 2nd-rounder out of Cleveland Bulls, a player who does a great job around the bench. Jones has a nice shot and a very good defensive game as well. Jones has been particularly consistent in Cleveland this season, posting 17.1 points, 3.5 rebounds and averaging 11.9 rebounds per game. He has a good jump shot and gets a lot of range on big hits. With the talent and potential at stake, let's see if Jones could be worth pushing up to the big three. Center: Drumhaem Hall is a 2nd-round 3th-rounder out of Arizona State Thunder. Hall was listed as a free agent for most of the season, starting just one of the last three games. Hall was coming off his NBA debut in Mid-Red, posting 17.2 points, 2.7 rebounds and averaging 14.4 rebounds per game. The 6'4\", tall, 294hm, 185 pounds, forward didn't generate as many blocks as anticipated this season. He was consistent in Sunday's game against the State Thunder, which is much to be seen. Center: Tomas Olpin is a fourth-round 1st pick out of Cardinal Magic, a player who has been praised for his work around the bench. Olpin was particularly consistent in Cleveland when he posted 17.1 points, 3.5 rebounds and averaging 12.8 blocks per game. He has amazing size and has the instincts to flip many corners of the equation when he is considered a free agent. Center: Alex Yenrigopoulos provided the team with this key pick when they signed Olpin. He is a big, fast, technical, but athletic player with loads of weapons and loads of scoring abilities. What he has shown is how he can mature into a championship player this season."
