        "text": "In the last few months, we've been working with a number of developers to get some big things done. The most recent of those is the release of a Decima on-demand feature for the Xbox 360, spearheaded by Miri Kaichka. Along the way, we've added tons of other new features to it, including the changes to the user interface for Etsuen, a bunch of things we've spent a lot of time working on during the campaign, to make sure it doesn't fall into too much limbo. And overall, the things we've worked on during the campaign are still very different than they've been before. It's goes without saying that we do still have a lot of work to do, aside from refining the graphics, making improvements to the graphics, and finally making things work for smart phones. It's best to make some minor changes, as we don't intend to do them before the end of the day. Instead, we want to make sure as many games as possible, whether for consoles, mp3 devices or third-party tablets, can reach a wide range of audiences across Windows phones and other platforms. We've got a lot of work under way for hardware integration, and we'd love to see how we can do it as soon as possible. But if we can continue to use the time and resources toward hardware integration -- we can, help us finalize how close we are to finalizing the games we want. We're still in a position to finalize what we're going to do, but for now, we're a long way from finalizing. We've been keeping in touch with our developers, and have been making some minor updates and fixes along the way. For example, we were going to kickstart work on a brand new campaign goal as soon as the game became available. We've also been making a couple of back-end updates to the campaign logo, which is one of the more important features we look forward to launch in coming months. Here are some minor changes that we are working on. First, there's a new building. Minor updates have been being made since we launched the campaign in the last few weeks, including minor changes to the campaign icon on the campaign website. In addition to the new building, a couple of minor updates have been made since we launched the campaign last month, including a minor update to the defining campaign logo. We've been working behind the scenes to make sure the game is available properly in the future, but we're doing everything we can to ensure it works properly in the future. We're also kicking off some minor pauses in the versions we've released in the last week or so to make sure everything starts properly. We've also made a few updates to the campaign website, including a minor renaming to Launcher's page URL, which contains campaign goals and campaign donations. In addition, we've renamed our page to include the campaign goals and campaign donations correctly. And finally, there's a minor update to the new campaign fundraising feature and a minor back-end update to the campaign website. The campaign web support page has been improved since the last update, but we're still doing everything we can to make sure it works properly in the future. So far, we've made a few minor changes to our interface, including an update to animation editor, and a new toolbar to the interface. We've also added the brand new Game Path feature, which will make the animation more visible. There's an animation plugin, and there are minor changes to some of the basic animation components to make them easier to navigate. We've renamed an animation panel for a message bar. We've added a new page renderer, a new animation engine for highlighting and highlighting items, along with a new plugin that will make the animations more visible. We've added a twist to page navigation and an additional twist to ad marketing. We've made a few other important changes, including the new live experiences feature, to make it easier for players to create their own unique experiences. We've also added a simpler story architecture to provide a more unique experience. For now, we've made a minor update to our Kickstarter campaign, which is something we're looking forward to launch in the coming months. Beyond that, here's a few major changes: As you go about purchasing the game, you'll be given the option to add the first few items to the bundle item list. Once you complete the campaign, after the game's content has been gathered, those items will be added to the bundle items for you to purchase later.."
